&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Brokerage Operations Associate I on Alpaca’s New Accounts team, you will work as an individual contributor supporting accounts-related work across the account lifecycle — onboarding, maintenance, updates, compliance-related cleanup, recurring operational projects, and initiative-based work across the function. You will partner with the New Accounts Principal Manager, owning recurring tasks and project work that strengthens the team and extends Alpaca’s account operations coverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, your week is shaped by the work in front of you — queue-driven tasks and recurring assignments at one moment, deep work in spreadsheets, exports, and data analysis the next — as team priorities evolve. You interpret what needs attention, drive items to resolution, and partner on focused cleanup projects alongside the New Accounts Principal Manager. The New Accounts team is 100% distributed and remote. This role reports to the Director of Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and support day-to-day accounts workflow throughout the account lifecycle;&amp;nbsp; onboarding, maintenance, updates, or closures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully own escheatment and abandoned property operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully own monthly statement and trade confirmation review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute legacy cleanup and data hygiene projects to meet compliance with CIP requirements, including partner and user communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work through spreadsheets, exports, and operational lists to identify issues, find patterns, and drive items to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Query databases at an operations level to identify and scope cleanup work, batch remediation, and measure progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside a team of New Accounts analysts on day-to-day processing, and support the New Accounts Principal Manager on larger cleanup initiatives (processing, data pulls, follow-through)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify repeatable processes from one-off and legacy cleanup project work, then drive those into ongoing workflows — making them more efficient or automated over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product, Engineering, Data, Compliance, and partner-facing teams to translate operational problems into actionable next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active FINRA Series 7 registration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of brokerage or financial services operations experience in one or more of: new accounts, account maintenance, CIP/AML, escheatment, statement review, or related account operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel or Google Sheets skills and comfort working from large lists, exports, and reconciliation-style work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of databases, tables, fields, and how data connects for direct operational data investigation for cleanup and solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently and able to take clear direction when available or interpret priorities and determine direction when it is not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong follow-through and ownership of assigned queues and projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for partner, user, and internal stakeholders communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail, accuracy, and reliability in a fast-paced, remote environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AML frameworks, sanctions screening, or identity verification workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency for a fintech environment (APIs, data terminology, basic system architecture) and comfort working with Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about Alpaca’s mission and comfortable supporting a global partner and customer base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-to-Haves):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FINRA Series 24 registration, or willingness to pursue over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with EDD, KYB, or business entity account support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeper experience with escheatment or abandoned property programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeper experience with statement review, trade confirmation review, or similar control workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in using AI tools to work smarter on drafting, summarization, and repetitive analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a B2B, API-driven, or correspondent brokerage model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
